+++ b/approved-adapter/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Approved biology adapter — isolated validation only
+
+This branch is based on production `biology-3`; it does not modify its render
+workflow, n8n, schedules, account, histories or locks. `candidate.patch` adds
+files to an immutable checkout of approved design commit
+`2a03f2954c379e5d9ef0d09ac616d8bcb560f5a8` in a read-only CI job.
+
+Implemented candidate families:
+- Protein coding nucleotides in one template DNA strand, 1..240 amino acids.
+- Chromosome number conserved by mitosis in a haploid fern gametophyte,
+  1..120 chromosomes, a two-step lesson. Other tissues/ploidies are rejected.
+
+The mitosis preview uses the condition and measured timing from a previously
+successful job, with identifiers removed. The source audio and n8n exports are
+NOT in this public patch. Its original voice was checked locally. No new TTS
+request was made. The preview is not a universally supported factory input.
+
+`elevenlabs-timeline.mjs` validates character alignment against the exact TTS
+transcript and existing segment boundaries. It provides exact phrase cues and
+inserts 2 seconds before speech plus 5.6 seconds within the measured gap after
+the condition. Playback stays 1x. Ambiguous repeated phrases, mismatched audio,
+wrong scope and durations exceeding 90 seconds stop processing.
+
+`prepare-audio.mjs timeline.json voice.mp3 output.wav` checks the source hash,
+decodes once, and preserves every PCM sample while inserting digital silence.
+It creates a manifest; there is no network operation, paid synthesis or upload.
+This is a voice preparation stage; the general sound-effects mixer is not yet
+implemented for the mitosis family.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run `node --test approved-adapter/*.test.mjs` for timing/sample checks.
+The CI workflow also checks frozen reference assets, original sound mix,
+17 full-resolution frames, and rendered mitosis layout/reveal/backward seek.
+
+Chromium may differ by one 8-bit channel level on a few pixels even when
+rendering two identical copies of the frozen source. The image gate records
+raw PNG equality and pixel statistics separately. It permits at most 0.01%
+of pixels to differ by at most 1 level, ONLY when the same-source control
+frame itself exhibits bounded rounding noise. Larger differences always fail.
+This is visual equivalence within a stated numerical tolerance, not a claim
+that all PNGs are byte-identical.
+
+## Not deployed
+
+The new scene needs human visual inspection of its rendered evidence before
+production use. Additional families (meiosis, endosperm, ATP, nucleotide
+percentages/mass) and automatic verified semantic scene selection remain to
+be implemented. Do not route arbitrary biology tasks to these two families.
+The production dispatch, callback, formatter and pacing guards are unchanged.
+Do not merge the entire experimental design branch into production.
